  "register": "documentary, and skeptical of the four-route map",
  "summary": "Pilgrims moved toward a shrine at the edge of Christendom on roads no one built for them, joined en route by rents, relics, badges, stories, settlers, and ordinary trade moving on the same paths in every direction. No pope, king, or order ever commanded the whole network — bishops, monasteries, town councils, hospitals, and shipowners governed their own pieces of it — and it did not end in 1520 so much as lose its medieval configuration under Reformation-era pressure, state regulation, and changing devotion, only to be rebuilt again and again afterward.",
